{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hypergraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A hypergraph is not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" and shares no parent protocol with one, because a hyperedge is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not an edge. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" module’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidenceGraphView"},{"type":"text","text":" reads a hypergraph as its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bipartite incidence graph (the Levi graph), which is how the graph algorithms reach it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedges"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every hyperedge once, a repeated one at each of its positions. A hyperedge’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position is its identity, as an edge’s is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions of the hyperedges a vertex is a member of, so a value keyed by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hyperedges.Index"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as a weight, is the same from every member. Positions are valid until the hypergraph is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With "},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" maps the vertices one-to-one onto"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0..<vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"incidentHyperedges(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read incidence in index space. With "},{"code":"hyperedgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"hyperedgeIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" maps the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions one-to-one onto "},{"code":"0..<hyperedgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so per-hyperedge state lives in arrays."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The algorithms in "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" need both bounds."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every conformer satisfies these laws:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexCount == vertices.count"},{"type":"text","text":", the vertices are distinct, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedgeCount == hyperedges.count"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The members of a hyperedge are distinct vertices."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a member of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedge at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", once, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedges"},{"type":"text","text":" order. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degree(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the length of that list and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of members, so the degrees sum to the sizes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"contains(hyperedge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly when some hyperedge has those members, the empty set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included. It and "},{"code":"contains(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" never trap."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is in index order, "},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"members mapped through "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same order, and the "},{"code":"(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads equal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertex reads."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With hyperedge indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedgeIndexBound == hyperedgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedges"},{"type":"text","text":" is in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"th position has index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Index-space members hash no vertex, and a vertex-space read looks its vertex up once.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Members with default implementations are still requirements. Generic code calls a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation’s own version when it has one, and a wrapper must forward every one. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol has no mutating members and does not refine "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph.swift#L39","fileName":"Hypergraph.swift"},"roleHeading":"Protocol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","title":"Hypergraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/Hyperedges-swift.associatedtype","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/IncidentHyperedgeIndices","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/IncidentHyperedges","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/MemberIndices","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/Members","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/Vertex","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype"],"generated":true,"title":"Associated Types","anchor":"Associated-Types"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/generation","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergr